1) data.csv is the baseline input data set for Workflows 1 and 2  with  approximately 10M vertices and 48M
   edges. data.stats gives the statistics for the standard data set. The data set includes one instance of
   the WMD pattern (see file patternRecords).

2) data.10.csv is a reduced data set approximately 1/10-th the size of the standard data sets. It includes
   the records of the pattern in the standard data set. data.10.stats gives the statistics for the reduced
   data sets.

3) data.200.csv is an expanded data set approximately twice the size of the standard data sets. It includes
   the records of the pattern in the standard data set. data.200.stats gives the statistics for the reduced
   data sets.

4) To compute the statistics for a data set, type

          python stats.py <data file> <output stats file>

   For example, data.stats was created by typing

          python stats.py data.csv data.stats

5) To generate a reduced data set from a data set, type

          python reduceData.py <data file> <reduced file> <reduction ratio>

   where <reduction ratio> is a real number (0.0, 1.0]. For example, data.10.csv was created by typing

          python reduceData.py data.csv data.10.csv .1

6) To generate an expanded data set from a data set, type

          python expandData.py <data file> <expanded file> <expansion> <seed>

   where <expansion> is a real number greater than 1.0. For example, data.200.csv was created by typing

          python expandData.py data.csv data.200.csv 2.0 0
